Package: unitTransformDist
Type: Package
Title: Generalized Unit-Interval Distributions via the Odds Transform
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mohamad Yamen", "Al Mohamad", email = "yamenmohamad@tabrizu.ac.ir",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ali Akbar", "Heydari", email = "heydari@tabrizu.ac.ir", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1236-3189")),
    person("Hossein", "Jabbari Khamnei", email = "h_jabbari@tabrizu.ac.ir", role = "aut"))
Description: Constructs, fits, and diagnoses continuous probability
    distributions on the open interval (0,1), obtained from an arbitrary
    base distribution on (0, Inf) via the odds-inverting transform
    Y = 1 / (1 + X). Unlike registry-restricted implementations, the base
    distribution is supplied directly as density/CDF/quantile/random-generation
    functions, so the package works with any distribution the user can write
    down, including custom research distributions with no closed-form
    quantile function. Provides maximum likelihood, L-moment, and Bayesian
    estimation; a corrected profile-likelihood confidence interval that
    re-optimizes nuisance parameters at every grid point (rather than
    holding them fixed); Monte Carlo simulation utilities for studying
    estimator bias, mean squared error, and confidence interval coverage;
    and multiple bias-correction methods (analytic, jackknife, bootstrap,
    median-unbiased, Firth-type penalized likelihood, double bootstrap).
